\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\fi360\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Falling to my death is not the way I thought my life would end. But here I am falling face first to the earth with no parachute.  As I get closer to my final resting place I start to recognize the scene below. I\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92m over the River. The thick cypress trees and crescent shaped rock formation signaled a familiar place. I don\u8217\'92t want to die here. Not here. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Ask and you shall receive I guess. In a second I realized my swift plunge had slowed. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 I am floating like a dandelion on the  breeze until I end up hovering over the water. Theres something moving just below the surface. Make that someone.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i1
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 The details of the person\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s face were hard to see through the water.  Long dark hair floated around like a graceful shadow as she looked all around. The woman\u8217\'92s outstretched arms frantically searched for something.  A way out?  A hand stretched in my direction and I realized that she was reaching for me. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 I\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92m terrified but I can\u8217\'92t just leave her to a watery grave.  I stretched my arm out toward her until our fingertips met. The cloudy water started to clear just as my fingers broke the surface. Then as if I have tripped an alarm an loud beeping starts.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn gasped and coughed she sat up in bed. She was in her bed. In her room. Safe. The digital clock on her dresser read 8:16. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93At least I didn\u8217\'92t oversleep today\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Knock Knock Knock}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Are you up?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn realized she was grasping the ring that hung around her neck. Something she often did when she was scared or uneasy.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Uh Um Yeah. I\u8217\'92ll be out in a minute.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Are you ok?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93You sound strange\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn took a deep calming breath before replying. Violet was a great room mate and even better friend. But sometime it was had to believe they were the same age violet was almost as overprotective as a Father on prom night. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Vi I\u8217\'92m fine. Not everyone can be like you in the mornings Susie Sunshine.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Fine\u8221\'94 Violet laughed But muffins are fresh out of the oven and I need a taste tester.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Mmmm.\u8221\'94\u8221\'94 Ok but give me a few minutes ready for work first.\u8221\'94 Said Autumn  \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m like 80 percent sure Allen is gonna fire me if I\u8217\'92m late again. Autumn responded}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I hopped out of bed and headed for the bathroom down the hall.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Violet was attempting to perfect her cranberry orange flavored muffins this week. And since Violet was an amazing cook Autumn had no problem being the taste tester.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Twenty minutes later Autumn sat across the table from her best friend. The house that they shared was small but did include a breakfast nook with a bay window overlooking the front yard. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Hows you head? Vi asked }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Oh much better. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn had over heated about two weeks ago and passed out in the front yard. Thankfully Violet had left work early and found her near the front steps. When Autumn woke up someone was playing a cymbal inside her head and shining a police search light in her eyes. Autumn had hit her head when she fell. Vi insisted on taking her to the hospital but that was a no go. Autumn would rather crawl over hot coals than go to a hospital. The compromise was Violet making a terrible herbal remedy. It smelled like sweaty onions and old potatoes but it did the trick. Autumn felt great. The only lingering affect was these strange dreams but she didn\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92t dare mention them to Vi for fear of another herbal fix.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I better get going Autumn said rising from her seat. She tilted the cup back to finish her orange juice before sitting it in the sink.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Good thing muffins were great for breakfast on the go. Autumn took another bite as she walked out the door.  The roses she and Vi had planted near the front door were looking great. A few red buds where already showing life. Autumn had alway seemed to have a green thumb. Even as a child planting things that could grow and produce something beautiful had fascinated her.  As an adult Autumn kind of liked to think of herself as a flower that could produce beauty in her artwork. Artwork that one day would be appreciated. }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0  But for now Autumn hopped in her blue Honda hatchback and headed off to work.  The homemade breakfast confection perfumed the cabin. The smell of oranges always made her feel happy. But anything that Violet cooked had that effect. }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 It happened so suddenly. Just as she started to cross Webb Creek there was a loud }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 Bang}{\f2\fs24\b0\i0  and the steering wheel jerked to the right. On a reaction Autumn pulled to left. Over correcting made things worse. Thank goodness she didn't end up in the creek. The guard rail stopped the Honda\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s forward progress. But the sudden stopped caused her head to bang the driver side window and then everything went black.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \tx0\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\fi360\ltrch\loch {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 The smell of disinfectant and hand sanitizer filled her nose as she tried to gain her bearings.  Looking around the room, Autumn clutched the silver ring that alway hung from the gold chain around her neck It took a few blinks to focus in the dimly lit room. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 A hospital?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Why\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8230\'85}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Suddenly Autumn\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s sluggish mind coughed up the events of the day. It was like a slide show was playing in her mind. She remembered donning her U-Store It t-shirt, grabbing her backpack and a muffin and heading out the door.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn! I\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92m so glad you\u8217\'92re ok. Violet said as she rushed to the side of the hospital bed. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Violet sat on the bed and quickly wrapped her arms around Autumn. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Oh Autumn I was so worried. Doug called and said you never made it to work. I\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92m so sorry that this happened to you. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92m alright. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I think I\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92m alright. No broken bones at least. Besides if was an accident.  I think my tire blew.  I guess I waited too long to replace them. I\u8217\'92m just glad no one else was hurt.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 So am I said Violet.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 How long have I been here?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 You left for work at 8:30 and the hospital called me around 10.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 What time is it now?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Just after 5:00.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 You\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92ve been here all day?}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Of course. Thats what family is for.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 She and Violet were not related by blood but had formed a bond as close as sister.  Autumn had been looking for a new roommate and Violet found one of her flyers.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Talk about bad luck. Autumn had lost her keys, nearly set fire to the breakroom at work. Now this car accident. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 In walked a tall thin man in a long white coat.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Good afternoon Miss North. I\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92m Dr. Moore. I am glad to see you\u8217\'92re up and alert.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Thanks. So when can I go home?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 We need to observe you overnight due to the head injury.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Autumn reached for the injury near her hairline and winced.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I feel fine Doc.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 25 years old with no pre existing health conditions. Im sure you\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92ll make a full recovery. But hospital policy for a head injury and loss of consciousness is an overnight stay.  ke}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Now I need to check out a few other things now that you are awake.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Thank you for being so thorough Doctor Said Violet}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Yeah thanks.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 You are very welcome Miss North. }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0       *** }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Jack gazed out over the hill at the sun rise. He knew the view extremely well. The same canopy of  trees. The same rushing stream that trickled it\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s way down the mountain. This was always the reward for his morning run. Hell just for getting out of bed before dawn. This view reminded him of why he worked so hard. But today he just needed time to think away from the rest of the guys.  Peace and quite.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Jack\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Hey Jack\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Well there went his quite.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Fuck. I don\u8217\'92t need a run partner or a baby sitter, Carver\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93I know you asked for space but the queen has requested an audience.\u8221\'94 Carver replied}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93When?\u8221\'94 Jack asked }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Now.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Alright. Has the Squad been informed?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93No. Said Carver. You don\u8217\'92t understand. The queen requested a private audience with you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Shit.\u8221\'94 Jack said through clenched teeth}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 And there went he peace.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 The queen had asked for a private meeting with him. She probably had finally gotten sick of his shit. Getting black out intoxicated wasn\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92t such a great idea. Especially when your whole reason for being was to stay alert and protect those in your care. Unfortunately losing someone in your care made it fucking hard to sleep. With sleep came the nightmares. The replay of that night that Jack would never forget.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 As they arrived at the Palace courtyard both Carver and Jack headed to the South lawn.  The palace stood on the north lawn. It had been built over 100 years ago to house the rulers of the race. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 On the south lawn just behind a grove of trees stood a two story carriage house in habited by The Squad.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 The Squad was a group of male Fae who protected their race. A race that was not as close nit at they used to be.  Some Fae were not even aware of there magical heritage now. The Squad could trace their lines back for over one hundred years.  Unfortunately you couldnt choose your genetic lineage and the bloodlines of the Squad had been tainted.  Each and every male of the Squad had pledged to lay down thier lives for their queen without question or hesitation. Queen Rayvn had reluctantly ascended to the thrown after her mother was killed in the attack that started the war.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 After a quick shower, Jack headed to meet with Queen Rayvn. The queen was waiting in the oversized chair near a window.  As always she seemed a bit uncomfortable.  As if she didnt belong.  }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Hello my queen\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Hi. Its very nice to see you this morning Jack\u8221\'94 the queen replied }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Jack fell silent not knowing what to say next. The queen broke the silence.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93 I asked for you to come here because I need your help.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8220\'93Of course my queen\u8221\'94 Anything that you request is law\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 The queen visibly flinched at this.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 I apologize Queen Ravyn. I did not mean to -}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Please. There is no need for you to apologize Jack. Really.  As I said I need your help with something. I need you to retrieve a wayward Fae. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 She lives in the Hill Country as a human. This Fae is unaware of her heritage. Her name is Autumn and she\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8230\'85}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 The queen took a breath and turn away to gaze out of the window. The sun shone in around her creating an auburn halo around her coils of dark hair. Funny how Jack had never noticed this before. He had alway assumed that the queen had been named for her dark black hair but in reality her hair was a deep dark red. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 After a moment Queen Ravyn continued. She needs our protection. The queen grabbed an inconspicuous piece of paper from the window sill. I was visited by the elder Vervina about three weeks ago. She had a vision of this young Fae. The queen said revealing a printed black and white photo of a young Fae woman. She was kneeling next to a small boy with a toy truck in her hand. A fire truck. The boy was beaming as he admired what was obviously a new toy. And though only the Fae\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s profile was visible, Jack could see that she was beaming right back at the little boy. For a moment Jack felt his heat fall out of rhythm.  Probably from the beautiful display of caring. Jack had seen far to little of that type of caring in his life.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Forgive me Queen Ravyn, Jack said but are you positive that I am the one that you wish to send. I don\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92t know a lot about the young ones.}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Young ones?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Oh. The young boy in the picture is not child. Autumn volunteers at an orphanage called Rainbow Valley in the Hill Country. When Vervina visited me with news of her vision I asked her to draw a picture of the wayward Fae. Once we knew what she looked like were able to find her with the facial recognition software. This photo is from a news article about a Holiday toy drive at the Rainbow Valley orphanage. }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Jack eye the photo again and again his heart skipped a beat.  }
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 May I ask my queen, what vision of this Fae did Vervina see?}
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Vervina told me that the Dark Storm is upon us. And that Autumn is the only Fae with enough light to save the Fae race.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
